t or uniform-in-terminal-time rate and still allows unbounded intermediate columns.","citation_ids":["circuit-r2-26-cite-sign-smoothing"],"evidence_ids":[],"id":"circuit.sign_smoothing","kind":"claim","label":"Finite sign smoothing preserves the rooted value","locator":"03-classical-optimization.tex:220–254; eq:energy-l2-continuity, eq:scalar-near-optimal-smooth","source_id":"scalar-r2-26-source-qaoa-scalar","statement":"For a given minimizer, choose T<1 and then a sufficiently fine finite mesh N. At that fixed T,N, replace F_N=sgn(H_N) by tanh(kH_N). The independent final uniform-rounding coordinate gives P(H_N=0)=0, so this converges in L² as k→∞. For every error>0, finite T,N,k give a centered finite descendant output z with |z|≤1 and E(z)≥P_*−error; local maps are odd and smooth with polynomially bounded derivatives.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/circuit.sign_smoothing","relations":[{"derived":true,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/circuit.sign_smoothing","id":"field:fbcb441d75c941bd2ec16b8d9dea0fab221c41bbafff43a4f8c6e5733e1448ac","kind":"assumption_ids","owner_ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/circuit.sign_smoothing","semantic_class":"explicit_assumption_reference","source_field":"assumption_ids","to":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/scalar.paper_minimizer"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/circuit.classical_fixed_minimizer","id":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/edges/%5B%22circuit.classical_fixed_minimizer%22%2C%22circuit.sign_smoothing%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/edges/%5B%22circuit.class